Z||000000||CanadianGT||05-04-2001||11:55 AM||||I know that this is not fiero related, but I thought someone here might be able to help me. My friend has a IROC with a 350 in it and the fan  will not go on.  We know that the fan works, and we have replaced the fan relay, the coolant temp switch in the block, the coolant fan switch, and we have tried a differnt computer. IT still constantly will over heat since the fan will not come on. We have already tried the IROC message boards , (Were little help)  so I told him that I would give the Fiero Forum A try.  Thanks in advance everyone.<BR>Kyle||||reg||1
Z||000001||elfiero||05-04-2001||01:15 PM||||P.P.sI'm not archie but I'll try to help.<BR>1.start the car and turn on the A/C,it doesnt<BR>matter if there is freon in the system or <BR>not.2.using a test light,backprobe the dark green/white tracer wire at the fan relay.it<BR>should have power.if the fan still won't run<BR>back probe the black/white tracer wire at the<BR>relay with a piece of wire(16-18ga) and ground the other end.if the fan now runs,you<BR>have a bad ground for the relay.if there is<BR>no power on the green/white wire,try back<BR>probing with12V.if it now works,you just trace down where the power supply is inter-<BR>upted.good luck!P.S.this is much easier than<BR>it sounds-don't be intimdated,you can do it. <P>P.P.S.check the orange wire at the relay with<BR>the test light 1st,this should be hot at all<BR>times,if not test the fuseable links,I'll bet<BR>you have a broken one.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by elfiero (edited 05-04-2001).]||||reg||6
